`storyPassesFilter` only succeeds when the entry reported by the preview has `type === 'story'`. If the user navigates directly to a docs page (e.g., `?path=/docs/component-foo`) with active tag filters, and that docs entry is present in `filteredIndex`, this check evaluates to `false` and the code redirects the user to the first filtered entry instead of staying on the requested docs page. Change the check to also accept `type === 'docs'`:
```typescript
const storyPassesFilter =
  filteredIndex &&
  (filteredIndex[storyId]?.type === 'story' || filteredIndex[storyId]?.type === 'docs');
```

`reverseBuiltInUrlTagMap` is rebuilt from the module-level constant `BUILT_IN_URL_TAG_MAP` on every call to `serializeTagsParam`. Since `BUILT_IN_URL_TAG_MAP` never changes, hoist the reverse map to module scope so it is computed exactly once:
```typescript
const REVERSE_BUILT_IN_URL_TAG_MAP: Record<string, string> = Object.fromEntries(
  Object.entries(BUILT_IN_URL_TAG_MAP).map(([urlTag, internalTag]) => [internalTag, urlTag])
);
```
Then reference `REVERSE_BUILT_IN_URL_TAG_MAP` inside the function.
